1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,800
Bolivia's sky mirror costs a 60-to-80-dollar tour. I'm your China Travel Expert.

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:05,200
That's Salar de Uyuni — the flat that mirrors the sky.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,600
Remote, bucket-list, and you need a guided tour to reach it.

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:10,000
China has its own sky mirror: Chaka Salt Lake.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,400
Entry? 60 yuan. About eight dollars.

6
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:15,000
A bullet train from Xining gets you there in an hour, 34 yuan.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,400
Same trick: still water, salt-white ground, endless sky.

8
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:20,000
Double-tap if you'd walk on China's for eight bucks.

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,400
It sits 3,059 metres up; the mirror pops after rain.

10
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:25,400
★ Expert Tip: go on a calm, clear morning after rain for the reflection.

11
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:28,200
Uyuni or Chaka — which sky mirror are you booking? Comment.
